[Expected Approach] Direct Formula Method - O(log(n)) Time and O(1) SpaceAn efficient solution to solve the sum of geometric series where first term is a and common ration is r is by the formula :- sum of series = a(1 - rn)/(1 - r). Where r = T2/T1 = T3/T2 = T4/T3 . . .  Here T1, T2, T3, T4 . . . ,Tn are the first, second, third, . . . ,nth terms respectively.  Consider we have n = 5, a = 2 and r = 2.Series is 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 which sum up to 62 = 2 * (25 - 1) / (2 - 1).    
            C++

    #include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

// function to calculate sum of
// geometric series
int sumOfGP(int n, int a, int r)
{

    // if common ratio is 1, the series 
    // is simply a, a, a, ...(n times)
    if (r == 1)
    {
        return a * n;
    }

    // applying standard geometric series 
    // formula : a * (r^n - 1) / (r - 1)
    return (a * (pow(r, n) - 1)) / (r - 1);
}

// driver code
int main()
{
    int a = 3;  
    int r = 2;  
    int n = 3;  

    cout << sumOfGP(n, a, r);
    return 0;
}


